+```text
+Distributed CrypTen deployment (staging/pilot)
+
+Quick steps
+1) Ensure crypten-worker image (ghcr.io/<org>/crypten-worker:latest) is built and pushed.
+2) Ensure crypten-mtls secret contains certs for pods (create from generate_mtls.sh outputs).
+3) Apply manifests:
+   kubectl apply -f ops/secure_agg/production_mpc/k8s/crypten-headless-service.yaml
+   kubectl apply -f ops/secure_agg/production_mpc/k8s/worker_statefulset.yaml
+   kubectl apply -f ops/secure_agg/production_mpc/k8s/crypten-rbac.yaml
+4) Wait for pods to be ready, then run:
+   bash ops/secure_agg/production_mpc/launch_distributed.sh aegis crypten-worker
+5) Tail logs: kubectl -n aegis logs statefulset/crypten-worker -l app=crypten-worker
+
+Notes:
+- This is a staging/pilot helper. For production, the worker image should start crypten worker process directly using proper entrypoint and readiness probes.
+- Use real CA and mTLS certs from your PKI; do not use the test CA in production.
